<section>
  <h2>Page object pattern</h2>

  <p class="mt-200r fragment">
    Page objects abstract away the technical interactions from the decision code
  </p>

  <if-pw>
    <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      await page.locator('.basket-mini .dropdown-toggle').click()  // this is about HTML
    </code></pre>
    <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      await cataloguePage.displayMiniBasket();                     // this is about the
                                                                   // application
    </code></pre>
  </if-pw>

  
  <!--
  "divide business-oriented decisions, workflows and technical interactions into separate layers."


  |  test layer   |  worfklow component        | technical interaction layer |
  |  - decisions  |  - manipulate page ojects  | -                           |
  |               |                            |



business decision layer:     | test 1 | test 2 | test 3 | ...                  |
worflow layer:               | worflow component 1 | worflow component 2 | ... |
technical interaction layer: | page object 1 | page object 2 | ... | Api client | Api client | ...| 
application:                 | UI                                  | API       |                   |

maybe mermaid's block diagram can help, or simply flex boxes...
-->
  <if-cy>
    <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      cy.get('.basket-mini .dropdown-toggle').click()  // this is about HTML
    </code></pre>
    <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      cataloguePage.displayMiniBasket();               // this is about the
                                                       // application
    </code></pre>
  </if-cy>

  <p class="mt-150 fragment">
    Tests with Page Objects are <strong>easier to read</strong> and
    <strong>easier to maintain</strong>
  </p>
</section>
